{"base_rate":0.5363276089828269,"brier":0.20800171730515188,"bss":0.16357784163473832,"bss_hi":0.25662127971611925,"bss_lo":0.058991948358276126,"country":"IE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1659313077939234,"ess":333.4528043775649,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Dublin</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Dublin rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>81%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>14%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nDUBLIN PHOENIX PARK, 4.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.16, ranked 14 of\n15 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(10&ndash;14) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>145</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>33%</b></td><td class='num'>82</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'><b>25%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>63%</td><td class='num'><b>67%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>85%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>95%</td><td class='num'><b>73%</b></td><td class='num'>81</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>81%</b></td><td class='num'>232</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Dublin\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.440413793103446,376.9793103448276 99.57341463414633,315.4146341463415 180.82868421052632,214.3684210526316 282.39373134328355,110.35820895522386 357.9432432432433,47.51351351351349 396.0044444444444,18.0 411.8321551724138,18.0 411.8321551724138,19.568965517241395 396.0044444444444,53.950617283950635 357.9432432432433,101.62162162162161 282.39373134328355,197.28358208955223 180.82868421052632,295.7894736842105 99.57341463414633,364.2439024390244 59.440413793103446,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"186.776750330251\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"186.776750330251\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.440413793103446,329.28275862068966 99.57341463414633,262.1463414634146 180.82868421052632,291.0 282.39373134328355,137.52238805970148 357.9432432432433,150.81081081081084 396.0044444444444,116.8641975308642 411.8321551724138,87.0344827586207\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 14% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 145 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.440413793103446\" cy=\"329.28275862068966\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 12%&amp;#10;It rained 33% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 82 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"99.57341463414633\" cy=\"262.1463414634146\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 35%&amp;#10;It rained 25% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"180.82868421052632\" cy=\"291.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 63%&amp;#10;It rained 67% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"282.39373134328355\" cy=\"137.52238805970148\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 85%&amp;#10;It rained 64% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"357.9432432432433\" cy=\"150.81081081081084\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 95%&amp;#10;It rained 73% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"396.0044444444444\" cy=\"116.8641975308642\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 81% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 232 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.8321551724138\" cy=\"87.0344827586207\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(54%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Dublin the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.18) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.09).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>58%</td><td class='num'>0.091</td><td class='num'>14.9%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>52%</td><td class='num'>0.091</td><td class='num'>18.6%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'>0.140</td><td class='num'>19.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>69%</td><td class='num'>0.183</td><td class='num'>15.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":53.3498,"lon":-6.2603,"n":757,"n_cities":15,"name":"Dublin","offset_days":1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00406896551724138,"n":145,"obs":0.14482758620689656,"sig":true},{"hi":0.2380000000000004,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.1174390243902439,"n":82,"obs":0.32926829268292684,"sig":true},{"hi":0.4740000000000003,"lo":0.2380000000000004,"mean":0.34697368421052627,"n":76,"obs":0.25,"sig":false},{"hi":0.78,"lo":0.4740000000000003,"mean":0.6338805970149254,"n":67,"obs":0.6716417910447762,"sig":false},{"hi":0.92,"lo":0.78,"mean":0.8472972972972973,"n":74,"obs":0.6351351351351351,"sig":true},{"hi":0.99,"lo":0.92,"mean":0.9548148148148147,"n":81,"obs":0.7283950617283951,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.99,"mean":0.9995258620689655,"n":232,"obs":0.8103448275862069,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":4.2,"rank":14,"rank_hi":14.0,"rank_lo":10.0,"reliability":0.030580223953825668,"resolution":0.07176747971242349,"slug":"dublin","station":"DUBLIN PHOENIX PARK","timezone":"Europe/Dublin"}